        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "豐津藩（とよつはん）"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Maru-marker opening the entry for Toyotsu domain, the 1869 reconstitution of the Kokura Ogasawara house (its castle burned in the 1866 Chōshū war) relocated to Toyotsu in Buzen. Everything from here leftward, down to the ○千束藩 marker, is Toyotsu's; nothing on this page lies to its right except the marginal running head."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "○豐津藩"
